WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.600
<i>Earthdash and the moon were born from the gods' ball game.</i> {recap}

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:09.850
<i>And between the two sibling planets, the same stone was divided.</i>

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.530
A stone laden with energy, ultinium ore...

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:16.760
...lingering remnant of the creation legend.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.950
The stars and planets were born in the gods' ball game.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.330
In their hour of need, the gods' power saves them.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.450
The giants' power.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.420
The great power.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.700
The legend.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:31.280
The savior in whose hands is the thunderbolt ball.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.910
The thunderbolt ball from the legend?

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:35.850
That's...

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.840
Bigfoots.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.360
Come to me!

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:41.890
Let's settle this,

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:44.860
basquashers!

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:48.950
Rainbow City, annihilated.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:52.200
Anakuz Town, 75 percent destroyed.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.050
Round City, annihilated.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.870
White City, 80 percent destroyed.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.790
Pearl Beach, annihilated.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:00.520
Seventown, annihilated.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.220
In addition, there are over thirty accounts of direct hits...

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:08.330
WHO ARE YOU?

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:06.970
...on highways and other evacuation areas, with great loss of life.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.920
Local stations report that even now...

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:38.850
Dan...

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.230
It's my fault, isn't it?

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:57.630
Gramps?

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:03.600
My son died and I came down to groundside.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.910
Maybe this is the bitter end of my penance.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:11.860
That might be.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:19.420
But there's nothing that says Slash's plan would've succeeded if you had stayed on the moon.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.360
It turns out that the legend never did appear.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:28.870
But these babies were born because my Gramps came down here.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:34.390
And I got to see Dan again.

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:40.720
See him operating the Dangan; something you, my dad, and I created.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.380
Miyuki...

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.900
I'm grateful to you, Gramps.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:50.710
I'm here now because you came down to earth.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.680
I'm glad I'm here.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.270
Thanks.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:08.320
We hereby convene the Legend League!

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:13.720
A moment in rememberance of our losses.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:16.130
Now, opening remarks by the League's organizer, Slash Keens.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:26.230
This League is truly the gods' battle reborn.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:30.950
Father?

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:33.710
Big brother... {alt tl: My older brother...}

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.210
The task entrusted to these players...

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.380
is to approach and surpass the gods.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:46.220
Until the thunderbolt flashes, and Earthdash and the moon are saved, they will not stop.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.310
This is cruel,

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:53.810
but how can it compare to the pain of all those who have lost their homes and families?

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.360
We'll pay whatever price you want!

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.790
Let us ride the Moon Cannon!

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.070
Take us to space!

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:02.590
Our borders are currently sealed.

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:04.030
You cannot enter the country!

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.950
More refugees have gathered at the borders.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.920
Use military Bigfoots if you want.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:12.020
Just make sure none of them get in before the launch.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:18.960
That's right... We may as well show them.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.510
Unblock the Mooneyes broadcast.

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:26.960
The loftiest and greatest project to save Earthdash and the moon,

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:27.800
the Legend League!

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:32.400
These baskets await more than just the impact of a ball.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.640
They await the thunderbolt's power — the ancient power of the gods.

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:41.110
These baskets are equipped with energy sensors.

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:45.230
They measure and digitize the energy hammered into the goal,

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:48.410
and update the legend candidate rankings in real-time.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:50.470
The same mechanism awards extra goals. {sz: "extra goal" — I'm guessing this is something like a free throw. This sentence is very short in the JP but I couldn't think of a shorter sub}

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:53.190
If baskets are made by thunderbolt balls,

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:59.130
watch the superconducting cables to see the flux in legend rankings as the match develops.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.800
If the legend gauge exceeds 100, {time from "densetsu geeji"}

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:07.700
that energy will be sent to the ultimite veins on the moon's farside

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:10.120
in the hopes they will be activated. {time from "kasseika"}

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:16.730
Regular baskets, by the way, are worth two points.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:20.100
An extra goal adds one hundred points in one shot.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.450
A hundred points?

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:24.940
We have to trust our lives to that?

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.170
{laughs} So the legend's power is worth a hundred points!

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:30.700
Interesting.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.280
You think the worst of people, General Manager.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:35.960
I'm showing everyone, aren't I?

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:37.120
What's wrong with that?

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:43.960
They should hate themselves for swallowing this banal little farce while their own demise approaches. {alt tl: while the moon is falling from the sky}

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:47.270
In the pits of despair, our plan will prevail.

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:51.300
The whole world will applaud you.

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.550
Applaud, will they? {laughs}

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:05.940
Stupid-head, I'm bored by myself.

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:09.790
Dan.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.770
We're here at the ruins,

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:22.290
but what happens now?

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:27.380
Lady Flora! Jiiya! Princess!

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:28.740
Baaya!

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:30.550
Oh, my wife!

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.880
You called a wind and flew here, didn't you?

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.330
You're incredible, Baaya!

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:36.720
Basquash.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.600
Who art thou? {alt tl: What manner of man art thou?}

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:45.490
The voice of the ruins, so loud and clear!

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:53.120
All four participating teams boast players with moves worthy of the name "legend".

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:56.130
Second-ranked in the League, the Silent Banes! {spelled "silent basins" in the sign, but let's ignore that}

00:07:56.130 --> 00:08:00.410
Watch their supreme playmaker, Doctor Oscarman, spinning out zero-g dunks!

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.800
Third-ranked, the Lunatic Gigantis! {spelled this way in the sign}

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.300
Their speed play, based on the philosophy of teamwork,

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:13.390
is truly like a lighting-flash! {lighting or lightning}

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.680
Next, the first-ranked Cosmostar Miracles!

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:23.770
Their captain, Milan Shefar, perfoms his Flashing Step!

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:27.520
He's called the man currently closest to the legend!

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:32.420
Hey, are those guys all using special effects for TV?

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:33.820
Like the BFB League?

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:37.950
By the way, the highlight reel of these players has not been altered in any way.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.420
Every single play is legend-class!

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:47.430
Last, we have the Toriena Heavens, here from groundside, by special request.

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:49.380
This team was thrown together in a hurry.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:53.380
Apparently they intend to play with only two members, and their reasons for doing so are unknown.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.430
Taking it easy with just two of you, huh?

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:58.560
Or are you just morons?

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:04.080
Let's have some fun, legend candidates.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:08.990
Shoulder to shoulder, all the Bigfoots have the bearing of heroes who have come through many matches.

00:09:08.990 --> 00:09:13.080
Which of them, which player, will throw the thunderbolt ball?!

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:16.410
Like I said, Miss Haruka, you should stand-by at the hotel.

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:18.950
If there's a message, then I'll tell Nike—

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:20.000
That won't do!

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.610
Delicate nuances must be conveyed directly.

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:23.560
It's all right!

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.240
I can handle Nike!

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:26.930
I'm the designer!

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:35.900
Nike, there's something I'd like to try out.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:37.570
If we can add ultimite to the sole materials—

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:41.260
I tried adding powdered ultimite to the sole.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:43.850
James!

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:45.940
Hey.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.100
Sorry, man.

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.590
We nearly got away with it... {sz: implies they were keeping "Nike-san's" identity a secret}

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:53.270
You two...

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.240
James, why are you...?

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.990
I wanted to understand you better.

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.200
How long?

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:10.130
When did I start, I wonder?

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:17.420
This street style can use the entire surface of Mooneyes!

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:20.660
Don't blink, because two matches will be ongoing simultaneously.

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:22.140
At long last, it begins!

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:23.480
Tip...

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:28.190
...off!

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:39.210
Come soon!

00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:40.780
I'm waiting!

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:42.340
Dan!

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:53.150
Alright! Alright!

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:55.010
Stop!

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:58.380
Miyuki and the others already left with Dan's Bigfoot for the ruins.

00:10:58.730 --> 00:11:03.960
I didn't have enough activated ultinium to finish more than one pair of shoes, though...

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:07.370
Your feet are liars, aren't they?

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:08.830
They never lied.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.370
They just kept silent.

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:13.240
One-two, one-two, one-two!

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:13.930
The two of us...

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:17.820
Neither one understood how the other really felt.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:20.780
The woman loved feet...

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:24.220
...and the man was loony for spheres.

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:30.170
Maybe those were our excuses for never really facing each other directly. {this show is so weird}

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:45.240
{bg}Blinding offense and defense... {continues illegibly}

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:45.930
What's happening with the Legend League?

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:47.550
It's <i>really</i> one-sided.

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:50.310
Really? But of course, it's Mr. Iceman!

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:52.570
It's the other way around. They're losing.

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:53.410
Iceman...

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:54.770
...And just look at that dunk by Milan!

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:55.730
No!

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:59.030
The top-ranked team in the Lunar League has wasted no time in...

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:02.110
...flooring the others with their rough welcome, time and time again!

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:07.450
What's wrong?

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:09.620
It's only just started.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:10.870
Low on oxygen already?

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:14.920
Don't underestimate the moon!

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:16.700
Go back to the surface!

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:19.580
Basquash, who art thou?

00:12:27.570 --> 00:12:28.420
Dan.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.260
Milan score yet again!

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:40.650
It's not even close.

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:42.650
Is Toriena Heaven's reckless strategy of playing undermanned...

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:45.450
...coming back to bite them now?

00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:59.970
The Cosmostar Miracles score another basket!

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:02.710
Where's Dan?

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:05.140
Mr. Dan?

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.590
Did he wake up?

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.430
He's not there, so I thought he must be here...

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.120
Then where?

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:19.400
Dan!

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:21.140
That's not him!

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:24.130
Miyuki?!

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:29.950
Is this really okay?

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:32.150
Doing this for real?

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:35.280
Miyuki!

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:36.500
Stop, Miyuki!

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:38.880
Bring Dan down! What are you planning to do?

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.370
Miyuki!

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:43.480
C'mon, Dan.

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:44.970
This is your Dangan.

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:49.180
He's been twice made new, so he's the New New Dangan...

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:51.660
...or something.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.930
You remember?

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:58.150
The first time you rode your Dangan?

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.570
He was waiting for you.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:05.530
Waiting for an operator who'd really let him rip.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:08.990
I was waiting too.

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:12.510
At the end of my search someone appeared...

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:16.570
Dan, that person was you.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:21.500
Basquash, who art thou?

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:25.210
What was that?

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:27.620
You heard it too, Miss Rouge?

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:28.510
Me too.

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.390
Me too.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:31.740
Me too.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:33.120
And me.

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:36.840
The voice of the ruins got louder again.

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:40.580
Basquash, who art thou?

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:42.610
Thy answer will open the door.

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:45.230
I'll take it this time too!

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:46.690
What?

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:52.810
I'd completely forgotten...

00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:55.920
I suppose I was as nervous as a normal man would be.

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:57.430
What are you talking about?

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:01.920
I'm a basquasher!

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.550
Destroy!

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:07.050
What?

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:08.930
What was that?

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:11.570
It's speaking!

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:15.530
Basquash, who art thou?

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:23.690
What's that?

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.220
Dan!

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:32.780
Mr. Dan!

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:40.950
Miyuki!

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:41.540
Dan!

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:49.530
Dan, time to shine!

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:52.390
You don't know what you're missing sleeping at a time like this!

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:55.670
Dan! Dan! Come on!

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:56.880
Stupid Dan!

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:03.040
Basquash, who art thou?

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:05.830
Thy answer will open the door.

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:11.240
Basquash, who art thou?

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:14.890
Thy answer will open the door.

00:16:16.570 --> 00:16:18.010
Basquash.

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:25.230
Who art thou?

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:48.150
This is awesome...

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:54.020
You're right, no way I could see something this awesome and not basquat...

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:54.780
Dan!

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.150
Stupid Dan!

00:16:56.150 --> 00:16:57.440
Here we go!

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:02.120
Basquash!

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:05.380
<i>nurui shakai nado shikato shite</i>

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:05.380
<i>Ignore the superficial ways this world works;</i>

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:05.380
<i>nurui shakai nado shikato shite</i>

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:05.380
<i>Ignore the superficial ways this world works;</i>

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:05.380
Iceman, take a look.

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:10.180
<i>bokura ga atarashii ruuru ni nare</i>

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:10.180
<i>we'll make our own new rules.</i>

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:10.180
<i>bokura ga atarashii ruuru ni nare</i>

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:10.180
<i>we'll make our own new rules.</i>

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:19.700
<i>hora! buchikowase kono te de</i>

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:19.700
<i>Look! Break it down using your own hands.</i>

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:19.700
<i>hora! buchikowase kono te de</i>

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:19.700
<i>Look! Break it down using your own hands.</i>

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:18.260
Dan!

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:26.840
<i>kimi ga kimi no mama motomeru basho wa doko</i>

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:26.840
<i>Where's a place where you can stay as you are?</i>

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:26.840
<i>kimi ga kimi no mama motomeru basho wa doko</i>

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:26.840
<i>Where's a place where you can stay as you are?</i>

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:25.220
Sorry I took a while.

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:28.660
Dan! Dan!

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:31.800
<i>dare no iinari ni mou naru na yo</i>

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:31.800
<i>Don't listen any more when people tell you what to do.</i>

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:31.800
<i>dare no iinari ni mou naru na yo</i>

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:31.800
<i>Don't listen any more when people tell you what to do.</i>

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:30.780
Dan!

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:41.040
<i>yume wa shinjiro furikazase</i>

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:41.040
<i>Believe in dreams and flaunt your power.</i>

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:41.040
<i>yume wa shinjiro furikazase</i>

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:41.040
<i>Believe in dreams and flaunt your power.</i>

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:35.260
Basquash, who art thou?

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:39.530
Hey! I dunno why you never shut up, but shut up and listen!

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:43.560
I'm Dan JD!

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:46.170
I'm the real deal! I'm a basquasher!

00:17:44.590 --> 00:17:48.790
<i>genkai o shiru ki nado zero da</i>

